The only change is to read `profile` into a local variable once. The compiler then doesn't need to reload the member after the bounds check, and the generated code is a little tighter. Behavior stays the same.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if (p == NULL)
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    const FIT_UINT16 idx = profileIndex;
    if (idx >= p->numFields)
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[idx].num;
}
```